# Agent Backend Configuration
# Copy to `.env`. Claude runtime (default) needs ANTHROPIC_API_KEY; the opt-in
# Pi preview runtime (KUHN_AGENT_RUNTIME=pi) runs without it.
# All values have defaults except the API key — see src/config.js for the full list.

# Model access (required). Alternatively, rely on Claude Code login credentials
# on a dev machine and leave this unset.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Pi live smoke (`npm run smoke:pi-runtime`): exercises the production Pi
# adapter against a non-Anthropic provider without spending Anthropic quota.
# The smoke never prints the credential.
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# KUHN_PI_SMOKE_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-20b

# Server port. For dev (two ports), this is the backend server (dev webapp is pinned to 5174).
PORT=3002

# CORS — allowed origins (comma-separated). The webapp dev server is pinned to
# 5174. Not needed for single-port deployments (webapp served by the backend):
# same-origin requests bypass CORS entirely.
CORS_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5174

# Built webapp served at / alongside the API (single-port deployment — see
# docs/deployment.md). Defaults to webapp/dist in the repo, served whenever it
# exists; set to another build directory, or to '' to disable.
# KUHN_WEBAPP_DIST=/absolute/path/to/webapp/dist

# Auth. Default mode 'dev' = no login (seeded dev user) — for
# local development. Set 'magic-link' on any shared/deployed instance; it
# requires a session secret. With no SMTP URL, sign-in links are printed to
# the server console instead of emailed.
#
# 'magic-link' is INVITE-ONLY: an address that already belongs to an org gets
# a sign-in link, and everyone else is queued as an access request for a
# super-admin to review — no account is created. See docs/deployment.md.
# KUHN_AUTH_MODE=magic-link
# KUHN_SESSION_SECRET=<openssl rand -hex 32>
# KUHN_APP_URL=https://your-public-hostname   # post-login redirect target
# KUHN_SMTP_URL=smtps://user:pass@host:465    # unset = console-log delivery

# Site super-admins, comma-separated
# Super admins can create, rename, and suspend orgs via the admin console.
# These emails are synced into the database at every boot (listed emails 
# gain the flag, unlisted lose it). In dev mode this defaults to the dev user; 
# in production there is no default, so without it nobody can create orgs.
# KUHN_SUPERADMIN_EMAILS=you@example.com

# How long org-invitation links stay valid (default 7 days).
# KUHN_INVITE_TTL_MS=604800000

# Rate limits on the sign-in form (POST /api/auth/request-link) — the only
# unauthenticated endpoint that sends mail and writes rows. Per-email is the
# limit that matters (it is keyed on the address being mailed, so it cannot be
# sidestepped); per-IP is best-effort only, since req.ip comes from
# X-Forwarded-For under `trust proxy`. Raise the per-IP cap if your users
# share one outbound address. Defaults shown.
# KUHN_LOGIN_MAX_PER_EMAIL=3
# KUHN_LOGIN_EMAIL_WINDOW_MS=900000
# KUHN_LOGIN_MAX_PER_IP=20
# KUHN_LOGIN_IP_WINDOW_MS=3600000

# Data directory: in-process SQLite DB (db/kuhn.sqlite) + uploaded project files
# (files/<projectId>/) both live here. Defaults to the repo-root ./data (gitignored).
# KUHN_DATA_DIR=/absolute/path/to/data

# Override the DB file path alone, or the project-files root alone, if needed:
# KUHN_SQLITE_PATH=/absolute/path/to/kuhn.sqlite
# PROJECTS_ROOT=/absolute/path/to/files

# --- Opt-in Pi runtime preview (STH-47) -----------------------------------
# Selects the model-execution runtime for every agent task. Default 'claude'
# keeps the Claude Agent SDK path. 'pi' runs the Pi AgentRuntime adapter with
# the explicit provider/model below. No silent fallback: if 'pi' is selected
# and Pi fails, the task fails with the Pi failure — switching back to Claude
# is an explicit operator change of KUHN_AGENT_RUNTIME.
# KUHN_AGENT_RUNTIME=pi
#
# Pi provider path: 'openrouter' (default) | 'openai' | 'google' | 'openai-compatible'.
# KUHN_PI_PROVIDER=openrouter
# The explicit Pi model id (Kuhn's per-agent Claude model ids are NOT used).
# KUHN_PI_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-20b
# Required for the 'openai-compatible' path (vLLM/Ollama/LiteLLM/...):
# KUHN_PI_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1
# Explicitly named credential environment variable (defaults per provider:
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY / OPENAI_API_KEY / GEMINI_API_KEY / OPENAI_COMPATIBLE_API_KEY).
# KUHN_PI_API_KEY_ENV=OPENROUTER_API_KEY
#
# Org model profiles (issues #107/#111/#112/#133): owners can add provider/model
# profiles (OpenAI, OpenRouter, Google Gemini, any OpenAI-compatible endpoint,
# or their own Anthropic key) under Settings -> Models, backed by org secrets, and route
# each agent to a ranked list of them by task difficulty. Nothing here is
# needed for that; the two knobs below bound it.
# Allow an org profile to point at a loopback / private-network base URL
# (a local vLLM or Ollama server). Defaults to true in dev auth mode and
# false otherwise — a private URL from the admin UI is otherwise an SSRF
# vector. A plain http: base URL is only ever accepted for such private hosts.
# KUHN_ALLOW_PRIVATE_MODEL_ENDPOINTS=false
# Time limit on the synthetic "Test connection" turn an owner runs from the
# admin UI (no project content is sent).
# KUHN_MODEL_TEST_TIMEOUT_MS=30000
#
# Platform-level pre-configured models (issue #138). Models every org should
# see without configuring them — a local vLLM/Ollama server, a site-licensed
# API key — declared once here as inline JSON or the path of a JSON file. Each
# entry becomes a read-only deployment profile (routable, testable) in every
# org's Models tab; an entry with `routes` is also the default route for the
# named agents ("*" = all) in orgs that configured none. Credentials stay in
# the environment: `api_key_env` NAMES the variable holding the key (omit it
# for a keyless local server, or to use the provider's default variable:
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY / OPENAI_API_KEY / OPENROUTER_API_KEY / GEMINI_API_KEY).
# Validated at boot — a malformed list stops the server with the entry/field.
# KUHN_PLATFORM_MODELS=/etc/kuhn/platform-models.json
# KUHN_PLATFORM_MODELS='[{"slug":"local-qwen","name":"Qwen3 27B (on-prem)","provider":"openai-compatible","model_id":"Qwen3-27B","base_url":"http://vllm.lan:8000/v1","capabilities":{"contextWindow":32768,"maxTokens":8192},"cost_weight":0.5,"data_policy":"Runs on-prem; nothing leaves the network.","routes":{"ra":0.5,"advisor":0.5}}]'

# Structured logging (STH-51): leveled console output plus an append-only
# NDJSON audit stream (agent job lifecycle, per-turn context-window state,
# file events, suggestion accept/reject decisions), one file per UTC day
# under <KUHN_DATA_DIR>/logs. LOG_LEVEL: debug|info|warn|error (default info).
# Set KUHN_LOG_DIR to relocate the audit files, or '' to disable the file sink.
# LOG_LEVEL=info
# KUHN_LOG_DIR=/absolute/path/to/logs

# Org secrets store: encryption key for org secrets at rest (32 bytes hex —
# `openssl rand -hex 32`). Unset = derived from KUHN_SESSION_SECRET (with a
# fixed dev-only fallback when that is also unset). Keep it out of DB backups:
# ciphertext and key must live in different domains (threat model TB-7).
# KUHN_SECRETS_KEY=

# Docker network joined by secrets-enabled analyst script runs (run_script
# with `secrets: [...]`) so sandboxed scripts can reach org data services
# (e.g. a Postgres container) by name. Create it INTERNAL so those runs still
# have no internet:  docker network create --internal kuhn-data
# SANDBOX_SECRETS_NETWORK=kuhn-data
